<title>USA: Jamaica gets $10 mln under PL480 for rice.</title>
<headline>Jamaica gets $10 mln under PL480 for rice.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Wednesday said Jamaica was authorized to buy $10 million worth of U.S. rice under Public Law 480, Title I.</p>
<p>USDA said the authorization provides for about 25,000 tonnes of long-, medium-, or short-grain milled rice or brown rice for processing in bulk.</p>
<p>The contracting period was set for Feb. 26 through Sept. 30 and delivery was set for Feb. 26 through Dec 31.</p>
